The AI update uses `ai.z` as a linear Z coordinate to find track center and curvature. This is fundamentally broken for a closed loop track.

A simpler approach than rewriting everything: use the track distance system. I can convert `ai.z` to be track distance instead of spatial Z. In initAI, the car's z is set to a stagger distance. If I treat this as track distance (along the path) rather than spatial Z, then the navigation functions can use `R.getTrackPosition(dist)` to get the actual spatial position.

But this requires changes to:
1. initAI - set ai.z as track distance
2. updateAISingle - increment ai.z by speed, use getTrackPosition to get spatial coords
3. getTrackCenterAt / getUpcomingCurvature - use track distance

