Actually, the simplest approach: rewrite these three functions to use `R.track.segments[i].dist` (cumulative distance) and `R.getTrackPosition(dist)` instead of linear Z. This is clean and correct.

Let me rewrite `getTrackCenterAt`:
```javascript
function getTrackCenterAt(trackDist, lookaheadDist) {
  const totalLen = R.track.totalLength;
  const targetDist = (trackDist + lookaheadDist) % totalLen;
  const pos = R.getTrackPosition(targetDist);
  return { x: pos.x, z: pos.z, curvature: pos.curvature, dist: targetDist };
}
```

`getUpcomingCurvature`:
```javascript
function getUpcomingCurvature(trackDist, lookDistance) {
  const totalLen = R.track.totalLength;
  const segs = R.track.segments;
  let totalWeight = 0;
  let weightedCurv = 0;
  const endDist = trackDist + lookDistance;

  for (let i = 0; i < segs.length; i++) {
    const s = segs[i];
    if (s.dist > trackDist && s.dist < endDist) {
      const weight = (endDist - s.dist) / lookDistance;
      weightedCurv += Math.abs(s.curvature || 0) * weight;
      totalWeight += weight;
    }
  }
  return totalWeight > 0 ? weightedCurv / totalWeight : 0;
}
```

And `getSegmentAtZ` should become `getSegmentAtDist`:
```javascript
function getSegmentAtDist(trackDist) {
  const segs = R.track.segments;
  const totalLen = R.track.totalLength;
  const dist = ((trackDist % totalLen) + totalLen) % totalLen;

  // Binary search for the segment containing dist
  let lo = 0, hi = segs.length - 1;
  while (lo < hi) {
    const mid = (lo + hi + 1) >> 1;
    if (segs[mid].dist <= dist) lo = mid;
    else hi = mid - 1;
  }
  return { segment: segs[lo], index: lo, localDist: dist - segs[lo].dist };
}
```

